     --CC      Clear the history buffer.

     --cc _s_e_t_t_i_n_g[,_s_e_t_t_i_n_g _._._.]
             Change the cursor appearance.  The change is specified by a non-
             empty comma-separated list of _s_e_t_t_i_n_gs.  Each _s_e_t_t_i_n_g overrides
             or modifies previous ones in left to right order.

             The following override _s_e_t_t_i_n_gs are available:

             nnoorrmmaall  Set to a block covering 1 character cell, with a configu‐
                     ration-dependent coloring that should be at worst inverse
                     video.

             ddeessttrruuccttiivvee
                     Set to a blinking sub-block with hheeiigghhtt scanlines start‐
                     ing at bbaassee.  The name “destructive” is bad for backwards
                     compatibility.  This _s_e_t_t_i_n_g should not force destruc‐
                     tiveness, and it now only gives destructiveness in some
                     configurations (typically for hardware cursors in text
                     mode).  Blinking limits destructiveness.  This _s_e_t_t_i_n_g
                     should now be spelled nnoorrmmaall,bblliinnkk,nnoobblloocckk.  A non-blink‐
                     ing destructive cursor would be unusable, so old versions
                     of vviiddccoonnttrrooll did not support it, and this version does
                     not have an override for it.

             bbaassee=_v_a_l_u_e, hheeiigghhtt=_v_a_l_u_e
                     Set the specified scanline parameters.  These parameters
                     are only active in nnoobblloocckk mode.  vvaalluuee is an integer in
                     any base supported by strtol(3).  Setting hheeiigghhtt to 0
                     turns off the cursor in nnoobblloocckk mode.  Negative _v_a_l_u_es
                     are silently ignored.  Positive _v_a_l_u_es are clamped to fit
                     in the character cell when the cursor is drawn.

             The following modifier _s_e_t_t_i_n_gs are available:

             bblliinnkk, nnoobblliinnkk
                     Set or clear the blinking attribute.  This is not quite
                     backwards compatible.  In old versions of vviiddccoonnttrrooll,
                     bblliinnkk was an override to a blinking block.

             bblloocckk, nnoobblloocckk
                     Set or clear the bblloocckk attribute.  This attribute is the
                     inverse of the flag CONS_CHAR_CURSOR in the implementa‐
                     tion.  It deactivates the scanline parameters, and ex‐
                     presses a preference for using a simpler method of imple‐
                     mentation.  Its inverse does the opposite.  When the
                     scanline parameters give a full block, this attribute re‐
                     duces to a method selection bit.  The bblloocckk method tends
                     to give better coloring.

             hhiiddddeenn, nnoohhiiddddeenn
                     Set or clear the hidden attribute.

             The following (non-sticky) flags control application of the
             _s_e_t_t_i_n_gs:

             cchhaarrccoolloorrss
                     Apply bbaassee and hheeiigghhtt to the (character) cursor's list of
                     preferred colors instead of its shape.  Beware that the
                     color numbers are raw VGA palette indexes, not ANSI color
                     numbers.  The indexes are reduced mod 8, 16 or 256, or
                     ignored, depending on the video mode and renderer.

             mmoouusseeccoolloorrss
                     Colors for the mouse cursor in graphics mode.  Like
                     cchhaarrccoolloorrss, except there is no preference or sequence;
                     bbaassee gives the mouse border color and hheeiigghhtt gives the
                     mouse interior color.  Together with cchhaarrccoolloorrss, this
                     gives 2 selection bits which select between only 3 of 4
                     sub-destinations of the 4 destinations selected by
                     ddeeffaauulltt and llooccaall (by ignoring mmoouusseeccoolloorrss if cchhaarrccoolloorrss
                     is also set).

             ddeeffaauulltt
                     Apply the changes to the default settings and then to the
                     active settings, instead of only to the active settings.
                     Together with llooccaall, this gives 2 selection bits which
                     select between 4 destinations.

             sshhaappeeoonnllyy
                     Ignore any changes to the bblloocckk and hhiiddddeenn attributes.

             llooccaall   Apply the changes to the current vty.  The default is to
                     apply them to a global place and copy from there to all
                     vtys.

             rreesseett   Reset everything.  The default is to not reset.  When the
                     llooccaall parameter is specified, the current local settings
                     are reset to default local settings.  Otherwise, the cur‐
                     rent global settings are reset to default global settings
                     and then copied to the current and default settings for
                     all vtys.

             sshhooww    Show the current changes.

